-- 152 -- **THE OTHER SIDE OF THE LAYOUT FACTOR: the byte pool, direct.**
--
-- The same byte API as `151-word-pool-discipline.gab` (read a byte, write a
-- byte, neighbouring bytes survive), but the storage is a byte carrier itself:
-- `static mut BYTES : [u8; POOLBYTES]`, indexed directly by `i`. No shift, no
-- mask, no `u32(255)` -- and the checker is still silent (`0 errors, 0 hints`).
--
-- THE PRICE IS IN THE EMITTED C, per access. A direct index into a byte carrier
-- is not a shape the emitter re-derives a bound for (`ausdruck_obergrenze`
-- covers a bare `index into T`, `x & MASK` and `x >> N` -- a bare ranged `i`
-- is none of them), so every access carries the emitter's second opinion, a
-- run-bound check (`leseBytes`/`schreibBytes`):
--
--     return ((uint64_t)(i) < 4096u ? BYTES[(uint64_t)(i)] : (__builtin_trap(), (uint8_t)0));
--
-- -- 79 characters of C where 151 emits `WPOOL_speicher.slots[w].w` (25): x3.16
-- -- per read, measured character by character; the write is a three-line
-- -- bind-check-store block where 151 emits one assignment. At -O0 and at -O2
-- -- alike (the check survives optimisation; both levels compute the same
-- -- answers -- measured, see MUSE-REPORT-237). The static storage is identical
-- -- either way: 4096 payload bytes are 4096 bytes of bss in both files
-- -- (measured `.o`: 4096 bss both; text 246 vs 202 bytes -- the word side pays
-- -- its arithmetic in code, the byte side in the branch).
--
-- So the two files are the two answers to one question, and the trade is
-- written down instead of hidden: 151 proves the bound ONCE (in the checker,
-- over `i >> 2`'s range, held by M103) and emits plain accesses at 14/24 ops;
-- 152 proves nothing per access in the checker beyond the declaration and pays
-- a bound check per access at 2/3 ops of Gabbro cost but ~4x the emitted C.
-- Where a pool is read on every packet, that is the number that decides.
module beispiel152 {

pub const POOLBYTES : u32 = 4096;

pub static mut BYTES : [u8; POOLBYTES] = 0;

pub lock BSPERRE protects { BYTES } rank 0 held <= 64 ops;

pub impl fn lies(i : u32 in 0 ..< POOLBYTES) -> u8
    requires Held(BSPERRE)
    effects { reads BYTES, locks BSPERRE }
    costs   <= 2 ops
{
    return BYTES[i];
}

pub impl fn schreibe(i : u32 in 0 ..< POOLBYTES, v : u8)
    requires Held(BSPERRE)
    effects { writes BYTES, locks BSPERRE }
    costs   <= 3 ops
{
    BYTES[i] = v;
}

}
